          <h3 class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-answer__pk-title">When should you pick Formester?</h3>
        </div>
        <ul class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-answer__pk-list"><li class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-answer__pk-item"><span class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-answer__pk-tick" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg></span><span><strong>Volume decides it.</strong> Responses are unlimited on every plan, free included. Jotform meters submissions monthly and Typeform meters responses.</span></li><li class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-answer__pk-item"><span class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-answer__pk-tick" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg></span><span><strong>More than one person builds the forms.</strong> 25 members on Business at $49. Jotform's paid tiers below Enterprise are single-user, and Typeform gives 3 seats on Plus.</span></li><li class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-answer__pk-item"><span class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-answer__pk-tick" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg></span><span><strong>You want payments before you pay.</strong> Stripe and PayPal fields work on the free plan, with no platform fee on top of the processor's own.</span></li></ul>
        <p class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-answer__pk-caveat">Skip it if a certificate is the requirement. Formester holds GDPR, UK GDPR, and CCPA, and is not SOC 2, ISO 27001, or HIPAA certified, so regulated work belongs on Jotform Gold or Typeform Enterprise.</p>
