    <section class="page-component-item">
      <div class="raw-html-content">
<section class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp" aria-labelledby="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp-title"><div class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__container"><header class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__header"><p><span class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__eyebrow">For developers</span></p><h2 class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__title" id="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp-title">Can AI agents read your form data?</h2><p class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__intro">All three ship an MCP server, so this is not a differentiator between Jotform and Typeform. What differs is the plan you need and what else is capped there. Formester includes MCP and the REST API on the $49 Business plan, with unlimited responses and 25 seats.</p></header><div class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__grid"><article class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__card"><span class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="16 18 22 12 16 6"/><polyline points="8 6 2 12 8 18"/><line x1="13" y1="4" x2="11" y2="20"/></svg></span><p><span class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__badge">MCP server</span></p><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__card-title">Let Claude, ChatGPT, or your own agents read submissions</h3><div class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__chips"><span class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__chip">Claude</span> <span class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__chip">ChatGPT</span> <span class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__chip">Custom agents</span></div><p class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__body">Jotform exposes mcp.jotform.com and Typeform exposes api.typeform.com/mcp, so agent access is available on all three products. Formester's is on Business at $49 a month, alongside unlimited responses rather than a monthly allowance.</p><p><a class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__cta" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://docs.formester.com/formester-mcp-server.html">Read the MCP docs &rarr;</a></p></article><article class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__card"><span class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 7V4a3 3 0 016 0v3"/><path d="M7 7h10l-1 7a4 4 0 01-8 0L7 7z"/><path d="M12 18v3.5"/></svg></span><p><span class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__badge fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__badge--alt">REST API v2</span></p><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__card-title">Or build on the REST API with a self-service token</h3><div class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__chips"><span class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__chip">Self-service token</span> <span class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__chip">Webhooks</span> <span class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__chip">Business plan +</span></div><p class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__body">Pull submissions into your warehouse, prefill forms from your CRM, or wire webhooks for created, updated, and deleted events. The token comes from app.formester.com/api in two clicks, no support ticket.</p><p><a class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-api-mcp__cta" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://docs.formester.com/formester-api.html">Read the API docs &rarr;</a></p></article></div></div></section>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="page-component-item">
      <div class="raw-html-content">
<section class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-switch" aria-labelledby="fmstr-cmp-jvt-switch-heading">
  <div class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-switch__container">

    <header class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-switch__header">
      <span class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-switch__eyebrow">Migration</span>
      <h2 id="fmstr-cmp-jvt-switch-heading" class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-switch__heading">How do you move from either one to Formester?</h2>
      <p class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-switch__sub">Three steps, and the same process works whichever of the two you are on.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-switch__grid">
<article class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-switch__step"><span class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-switch__num" aria-hidden="true">1</span><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-switch__title">Export your submissions</h3><p class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-switch__body">In Jotform, open the form's Submissions page and download as CSV or Excel. In Typeform, use the Results tab and export responses. Do it while the plan is active.</p><p class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-switch__hint"><strong>Time:</strong> about five minutes per form.</p></article><article class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-switch__step"><span class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-switch__num" aria-hidden="true">2</span><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-switch__title">Rebuild with AI</h3><p class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-switch__body">Paste your question list into Formester's AI generator or describe the form in a sentence. It drafts the fields, pages, and design in about half a minute, then you adjust wording and branding.</p><p class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-switch__hint"><strong>Input options:</strong> plain prompt, pasted question list, or PDF upload.</p></article><article class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-switch__step"><span class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-switch__num" aria-hidden="true">3</span><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-switch__title">Repoint links and embeds</h3><p class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-switch__body">Swap the embed or share link for Formester's, reconnect Stripe or PayPal if you collect payments, and send one test submission before retiring the old form.</p><p class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-switch__hint"><strong>Safety net:</strong> nothing counts against a response allowance while you test.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
      </div>
    </section>

