      <h2 id="fmstr-cmp-jvt-when-wins-heading" class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-when-wins__heading">When should you pick one of them instead?</h2>
      <p class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-when-wins__sub">Both win real categories. Three cases where Jotform or Typeform is the right answer.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-when-wins__grid">
<article class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-when-wins__card"><span class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-when-wins__cicon" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 1.5l2 6.9 6.9 2-6.9 2-2 6.9-2-6.9-6.9-2 6.9-2z"/></svg></span><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-when-wins__title">The respondent experience is the product</h3><p class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-when-wins__desc">Typeform's one-question-at-a-time format is the whole design, not a display mode.</p><ul class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-when-wins__list"><li>G2 reviewers praise its conversational design 88 times, against 21 customization complaints</li><li>Branching, calculations, scores, and variables are available on its free plan</li><li>Formester ships classic and card-style layouts, not a conversational thread</li></ul><p class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-when-wins__tradeoff">Choose Typeform when completion rate matters more than depth</p></article><article class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-when-wins__card"><span class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-when-wins__cicon" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14.7 6.3a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.4l1.6 1.6a1 1 0 0 0 1.4 0l3.77-3.77a6 6 0 0 1-7.94 7.94l-6.91 6.91a2.12 2.12 0 0 1-3-3l6.91-6.91a6 6 0 0 1 7.94-7.94l-3.76 3.76z"/></svg></span><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-when-wins__title">You need depth and volume together</h3><p class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-when-wins__desc">Jotform carries the wider feature surface at the lower price per response.</p><ul class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-when-wins__list"><li>Up to 1,000 fields per form, 40+ payment gateways, and offline capture with sync</li><li>1,000 submissions a month at $34, against $56 for the same volume on Typeform</li><li>Formester has no response cap but a smaller integration catalogue</li></ul><p class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-when-wins__tradeoff">Choose Jotform for high-volume, feature-heavy forms</p></article><article class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-when-wins__card"><span class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-when-wins__cicon" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 13c0 5-3.5 7.5-7.66 8.95a1 1 0 0 1-.67-.01C7.5 20.5 4 18 4 13V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1c2 0 4.5-1.2 6.24-2.72a1.17 1.17 0 0 1 1.52 0C14.51 3.81 17 5 19 5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1z"/><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"/></svg></span><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-when-wins__title">Compliance decides the purchase</h3><p class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-when-wins__desc">The two split here, and it depends which certificate you need.</p><ul class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-when-wins__list"><li>Typeform publishes SOC 2 Type II, ISO 27001, PCI DSS, and HIPAA in a live trust centre</li><li>Jotform reaches HIPAA far cheaper, on Gold at $99 a month billed annually</li><li>Formester holds GDPR, UK GDPR, and CCPA, and is not SOC 2 or ISO 27001 certified</li></ul><p class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-when-wins__tradeoff">Choose Typeform for certificate breadth, Jotform for affordable HIPAA</p></article>
