<section class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-privacy" aria-labelledby="fmstr-cmp-jvt-privacy-heading">
  <div class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-privacy__container">
    <div class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-privacy__inner">
      <div class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-privacy__text">
        <span class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-privacy__eyebrow">Privacy and data ownership</span>
        <h2 id="fmstr-cmp-jvt-privacy-heading" class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-privacy__heading">Who owns your form data?</h2>
        <div class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-privacy__body">
          <p>You do. Everything moving through your forms is Customer Data: the prompts you type, the structures the AI drafts, and every response someone submits. Section 4.4 of our Data Processing Addendum bars Formester from using any of it to train AI models, run advertising, or feed analytics and marketing. The Google Gemini integration that drafts forms works inside the same boundary.</p>
          <p>Responses travel over TLS, sit encrypted at rest, and payment data carries an extra AES-256 layer through Stripe. Formester is GDPR, UK GDPR, and CCPA compliant. We are not SOC 2, ISO 27001, or HIPAA certified, and the security page says exactly that instead of hinting otherwise. Compensating controls are in place: encryption in transit and at rest, annual third-party penetration testing, enforced 2FA, and encrypted backups.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-privacy__card">
        <span class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-privacy__pill">DPA &sect;4.4 &middot; January 2026</span>
        <blockquote class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-privacy__quote">"Formester shall not use Customer Data for purposes of analytics, advertising, marketing, or training of artificial intelligence or machine learning models, except as strictly necessary to provide the Services."</blockquote>
        <hr class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-privacy__divider" />
        <p class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-privacy__cite">Formester Data Processing Addendum, effective January 2026.</p>
        <div class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-privacy__links">
          <a href="https://formester.com/dpa/">Read the DPA &rarr;</a>
          <a href="https://formester.com/security/">Security overview &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </aside>
