<section class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs" aria-labelledby="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs-heading">
  <div class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__container">
    <div class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__header">
      <span class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__eyebrow">FAQs</span>
      <h2 id="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs-heading" class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__heading">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <p class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__sub">Everything else people ask when choosing between Jotform, Typeform, and Formester.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__list">
      <details class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__item">
        <summary class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__q">Is Jotform or Typeform cheaper?</summary>
        <div class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__a">It depends entirely on volume, and the headline reverses. Typeform's Basic is $28 a month billed annually against Jotform's Bronze at $34, but Basic includes 100 responses a month and Bronze includes 1,000. Matching Jotform's volume on Typeform means Plus at $56, making Jotform roughly 39% cheaper at that usage.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__item">
        <summary class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__q">Is Typeform actually free?</summary>
        <div class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__a">There is a free plan, but it allows 10 responses a month. Typeform's pricing table does not list the free tier at all, only a footer link. It works for testing, not for running anything.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__item">
        <summary class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__q">Is Jotform actually free?</summary>
        <div class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__a">Its Starter plan is free with 5 forms, 100 submissions a month, 100 MB of storage, and 100 fields per form. That is enough for a small real form, unlike Typeform's 10 responses a month.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__item">
        <summary class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__q">Which one supports HIPAA?</summary>
        <div class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__a">Both, at very different prices. Jotform offers HIPAA on Gold at $99 a month billed annually and on Enterprise. Typeform offers it on Enterprise only, custom priced. For a small clinic, Jotform is the reachable option of the two.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__item">
        <summary class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__q">Can I add teammates to a Jotform paid plan?</summary>
        <div class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__a">Not below Enterprise. Jotform describes Bronze, Silver, and Gold as 1 User Individual Plans, so multi-user access requires Enterprise. Typeform includes 3 seats on Plus and 5 on Business.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__item">
        <summary class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__q">Does either have an MCP server for AI agents?</summary>
        <div class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__a">Both do. Jotform exposes mcp.jotform.com and Typeform exposes api.typeform.com/mcp, so AI agent access is not a differentiator between them. Formester's MCP server is on its Business plan at $49 a month.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__item">
        <summary class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__q">Which has the better respondent experience?</summary>
        <div class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__a">Typeform, and the review data supports it rather than just the marketing. Its G2 reviews carry 88 mentions praising the conversational design, while Jotform accumulates 433 mentions across design and customization complaint themes.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__item">
        <summary class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__q">Where does Formester fit?</summary>
        <div class="fmstr-cmp-jvt-faqs__a">As the option when the thing you need is capped on both. Formester has no response allowance on any plan, includes 25 team members on Business at $49 a month, and puts payments on the free plan. It is not SOC 2 or HIPAA certified, so regulated work belongs with Jotform Gold or Typeform Enterprise.</div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
